let w = dataset(wages).where(year == 2019)
w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ + poly(exper, 2))
---- exit code 1
error[Z0103]: no function is called `poly`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:26
  |
2 | w.reg(log(wage) ~ educ + poly(exper, 2))
  |                          ^^^^ not a function of Zeff
  |
  = help: write the powers out: `exper + exper^2`; in a model with an intercept the fitted values are those of R's `poly`, and the coefficients those of `raw = TRUE`
  = help: for an ordered category, `category(x, contrast: poly)` gives the polynomial contrasts

